# systemd presets for policy mode MANAGED.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THIS FILE. A preset is a DECLARATION of what `systemctl preset` should do
# to a unit that has no enablement state yet. It does not change a unit that is already enabled or
# already disabled, and it does nothing at all unless something runs `systemctl preset`.
#
# So this file on its own is the textbook "configured but not effective" artefact that check B5 fails
# a mode for. It is shipped because it is the declarative statement of intent and because it is what
# governs units installed later -- and apply-policy ALSO runs the real `systemctl enable/disable/mask`
# for every line here, so the state on the built image is the state, not an intention about the state.
enable bootc-fetch-apply-updates.timer
disable debug-shell.service
